# Local credentials — a metresis read token, a store secret. Never committed.
*_token

# Editor artifacts, which are not hygiene here but a credential rule. An Emacs
# auto-save buffer named `#config#` was committed in 868743e carrying an exio
# access key and its secret — the buffer a secret had been pasted into, saved
# into the repository root under a name no pattern above matched. The package's
# `files` list meant it never shipped to hex, and the shipped-file guard in
# `mix_project_test.exs` only checks that LISTED files exist, so nothing
# noticed an extra tracked one. These patterns are what would have.
#
# `#` opens a COMMENT in a .gitignore, so the pattern for the artifact that
# actually caused this has to be escaped — `#*#` is a comment and silently
# matches nothing. Caught by probing the rules with a real file rather than
# trusting them, which is the only way this class of mistake surfaces.
\#*#
.\#*
*~
*.swp
